# nr-office-raster-canvas: the 2D canvas of the Office stack in mixdog-raster (module `canvas`, over tiny-skia), its recording and twin test.

The code of the task is in crates/mixdog-raster/src/canvas/{mod,path,paint,text,image_data}.rs and tests/twin_canvas.rs. It was written
without running cargo (the lead compiles the wave); nothing below is optional, the module does not compile without the dependency lines.

## native/core/Cargo.toml

[workspace.dependencies]: add, next to `ttf-parser = "=0.25.1"` (owner decision "2D rasteriser"; tiny-skia 0.11.4 with tiny-skia-path 0.11.4
and strict-num 0.1.1 are in the local cargo cache and already in Cargo.lock because resvg uses them; default features stay on, so the
lock does not change):

    tiny-skia = "=0.11.4"

## native/core/crates/mixdog-raster/Cargo.toml (dependency edges only; the crate is the raster crate's, the lines are this task's)

[dependencies]: add (alphabetical, before `mixdog-imaging`):

    mixdog-fonts = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-fsio = { workspace = true }

and after `mixdog-rt`:

    tiny-skia = { workspace = true }
    ttf-parser = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies]: add:

    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }
    sha2 = { workspace = true }

(mixdog-fonts does not depend on mixdog-raster and mixdog-office-base does not either: no cycle. tiny-skia exposes tiny-skia-path through
`tiny_skia::{Path, PathBuilder, Transform, ...}`: no direct edge to it.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-raster/src/lib.rs

In the module list add, before `pub mod composite;`:

    pub mod canvas;

and in the `pub use` list, before `pub use crate::composite::Blend;`:

    pub use crate::canvas::Canvas;

and in the module doc (first paragraph) add one sentence: "`canvas` is the 2D canvas the office code draws with (`@napi-rs/canvas`), over tiny-skia."

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Package mixdog-raster gets these dependency lines (the list is alphabetical; dev-dependencies are listed with the rest):

    "mixdog-fonts",
    "mixdog-fsio",
    "mixdog-office-base",
    "sha2",
    "tiny-skia",
    "ttf-parser",

No other package changes (tiny-skia 0.11.4, tiny-skia-path, strict-num, ttf-parser 0.25.1 and sha2 are locked already). Regenerate offline with
`cargo update -w`.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run the repository's hakari check after the edges are added; take its output if it asks for a line (tiny-skia and ttf-parser may be added to
the hack's dependency list).

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

Add to "sets" (keep the list sorted by set name; verify with benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs, which also recomputes the
manifestSha256 if the line endings of office-canvas/MANIFEST.json changed on checkout):

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-canvas.mjs --tree <dir with node_modules>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-canvas/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "8e715af7a57564cffee480ef0d44f03d4b4aac261165040b6695d2a96bbe9494",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-canvas.mjs",
      "set": "office-canvas",
      "totalBytes": 570551
    }

The set's MANIFEST.json records `product.commit: null` (the tree the recorder loaded, C:/Project/mixdog, has uncommitted changes under
src/ against its HEAD 0bf8fe045; the file counts are in the manifest). Re-record from an exact checkout with `--tree` when one is at hand.

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No name to remove: this task registers no service.

## Consumers (later tasks)

The PDF renderer (nr-office-pdf-render), the contact sheet (nr-office-authoring-contact-sheet), the visual diff and the rendered-page
metrics of mixdog-office-quality draw on `mixdog_raster::canvas::Canvas`, with `mixdog_raster::canvas::skia` for masks and shaders.
The font registry and the lane read proof reach `fill_text` / `stroke_text` / `measure_text` as arguments: the consumer owns the
`Arc<Registry>` it builds with mixdog-fonts.
